  "description": "meme-id: show_intolerance_for_others_religions; hasOverallIntent: Hateful; overall-intent-description: The image depicts a crowd of men, one prominently in the foreground with an aggressive expression, shouting and pointing, while others in the background raise their fists and hold flags. The text overlays state: 'show intolerance for other's religions' and 'expect highest level of tolerance for their own.' This juxtaposition is used to criticize and condemn religious intolerance, particularly when it is selective or hypocritical. The visual of the angry, shouting man is mapped onto the textual message to create a caricature of religious extremism and hypocrisy. The intent is to highlight and condemn the perceived double standard in religious tolerance, which can be interpreted as a form of religious bigotry or Islamophobia, as it implies that those who are intolerant of other religions are themselves intolerant of their own, thus framing the behavior as inherently hypocritical and hateful toward religious minorities or other faiths.",
